# {{ .DirName }} — sbx-kit catalog directory

This directory is a **catalog directory** managed by [sbx-kit](https://github.com/nkapatos/sbx-kit). It composes Docker **sbx** recipes from manifests, kits, and optional custom images.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `recipes/agents.yaml` | Recipe manifest (sbx-kit; interim format) |
| `kits/` | sbx kit specs (`spec.yaml`) — schema owned by **sbx** |
| `images/` | Custom Dockerfiles imported via `sbx-kit recipes image load` |

Recipe id: **`{{ .RecipeID }}`** (`<dir>/<name>`).

## Commands

```bash
sbx-kit recipes verify {{ .RecipeID }}
sbx-kit box run {{ .RecipeID }} --yes
sbx-kit recipes verify kits {{ .DirName }}
```

Recipe checks are done by sbx-kit. Kit checks are done by sbx (`sbx kit verify`). Migrate kits with sbx, not sbx-kit.

## Edit the starter recipe

File: `recipes/agents.yaml`

- `defaults.kits` — kits applied to every recipe unless overridden
- `agents.<name>.sbx_agent` — sbx agent kind (`{{ .SbxAgent }}` today)
- `agents.<name>.kits` — optional per-recipe kit stack
- `agents.<name>.image_name` — optional custom template tag

## Upstream docs (sbx)

Read these when authoring kits or images — not duplicated here:

- [Docker Sandboxes overview](https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/) — isolation, `sbx run`, when the box is the runtime
- [Customize: templates and kits](https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/) — template vs kit; kits are YAML applied at create
- [Editor integrations](https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/integrations/) — SSH, workspace paths, Cursor/VS Code over `.sbx`
- [Kit spec v2](https://github.com/docker/sbx-kits-contrib/blob/main/spec/SPEC-v2.md) — authoritative kit YAML schema

Global sbx-kit skill: run `sbx-kit recipes skill` and install under `.cursor/skills/sbx-kit/SKILL.md` if using Cursor.
